# THE PART OF _redirects THAT IS NOT DERIVED FROM .htaccess.
#
# Everything in out/_redirects below the banner is generated from .htaccess on every build. This
# file is what comes before it, and it exists because Apache's Redirect cannot say what these say:
# a redirect from an absolute URL on another domain, carrying its own status, forced ahead of any
# file that might share the path.
#
# `301!` is that force — the bang is Netlify's own way of saying "even if a file exists there".

# ufoathome.org used to be a domain of its own pointing at one page of this site, with the path it
# was asked for handed on as the observation to open. Its DNS now points at the tool's own Netlify
# site instead, so the two rules that did that could never fire again — a request for that host no
# longer reaches this one. The convention itself is not lost: that site answers an unknown path by
# opening its player on it, which is what these rules were for.
